+
+# Validate task title, priority and tags
+
+## Request
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, and odd tasks show up. The list should
+reject invalid input with a clear error that says what is wrong:
+
+- a title that is empty, or only spaces;
+- a title longer than 120 characters;
+- a priority other than `low`, `normal` and `high`;
+- a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+
+This applies when a task is added, renamed or tagged. When input is rejected, nothing in the list changes.
+
+## Feature and story
+
+- Feature: input validation on add, rename and tag in the Tidy Tasks list.
+- Story: as an app screen, I hand the list whatever the user typed and get a clear error back when it is
+  not valid, so that no odd task reaches the list.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+1. `add` rejects an empty or all-spaces title, a title longer than 120 characters, and a priority other
+   than `low`, `normal` or `high`. Each rejection is a failed result with the code `invalid-input` and a
+   message that says what is wrong.
+2. `rename` rejects the same invalid titles, and `tag` rejects an empty tag or a tag containing a space,
+   with the same code and clear messages.
+3. A rejected call changes nothing: the list, the task and its `updatedAt` are as they were.
+4. Valid input behaves as before.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- R1. The title is judged after surrounding spaces are removed, since that is the title the list keeps.
+  Its length limit is 120 characters.
+- R2. The priority check applies at runtime, since screens may pass a value the types do not cover.
+- R3. A tag is invalid when it is empty or contains a space character.
+- R4. Validation is done in the domain, returning a `Result`; no exception is thrown (directive r4).
+- R5. The new error code is added to `TodoErrorCode`; the doc comments of the changed exports say what
+  is checked.
+- R6. Tests in `test/list.test.ts` cover each rule and each rejected call leaving the list unchanged;
+  `npm test` passes.
+- R7. No new dependency; no clock or randomness in the domain (directives r1, r3).
+
+## Notes for the next steps
+
+- Choice made here: the code is `invalid-input`, a new member of `TodoErrorCode`.
+- Choice made here: only the space character `' '` is refused in a tag, as the request says; other
+  whitespace such as a tab is not checked.
+- Choice made here: the 120-character limit is measured on the trimmed title, the one the list stores.
